# Repo-wide invariants

This is a **personal knowledge repo** (Markdown + Cursor skills/rules).
There is no build, no test, no deployable artifact. Treat all changes
as documentation edits.

## Layout (top level)

```
AGENTS.md  README.md  .cursor/  knowledge/  papers/  notes/  weekly/  artifacts/  scripts/
```

Do not introduce new top-level directories without updating both
`AGENTS.md` and this file.

## Naming

- All new files & directories: **kebab-case**, lowercase, ASCII.
- Each directory has **exactly one `README.md`**. No `README_<x>.md`
  siblings.
- Progress note: `YYYY-MM-DD_HHMM_<topic>.md` (minute precision).
- Archive / paper note: `YYYY-MM-DD_<topic>.md` or just `<slug>.md` for
  `papers/`.

## Commits

- Never commit without an explicit user instruction.
- One logical concern per commit; never bundle unrelated edits.
- Imperative subject ≤ 72 chars.

## Tone & formatting

- No emojis anywhere unless the user asks.
- Prefer tables over bullet lists when comparing ≥ 3 things across
  ≥ 2 attributes.
- Cite paths with backticks, never bare.

## Hardware context (default unless overridden)

AMD MI300X / MI325X / MI355X (CDNA3 / CDNA4); ROCm + PyTorch; SLURM;
Podman container `xiaoming-dev`. Comparison reference is NVIDIA
H100 / H200 / B200. Do not assume CUDA-only paths; both ROCm and CUDA
matter.

## When unsure

Grep `knowledge/` then `papers/` then `notes/` before asking. Never
invent paper titles, hardware specs, command flags, or paths.
